attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le02ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Past vs Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Explanation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Action is over and has no connection to present \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use \u201ced\u201d for regular verbs.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Action happened in the past, but there is some connection to the present, action may still be happening in the present \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"use \u201chave or has\u201d and past participle of verb\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Indira Gandhi died in 1984. (Simple Past)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Indira has been a symbol of hope in India. (Present Perfect)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Indians saw her as the \"Mataji\". (Simple Past)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Some people have seen her as a dictator. (Present Perfect)", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Used to and Would to Talk About Past Habits", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you talk about routines in the past, you can use the expressions <span class =\"strong\">WOULD</span> and <span class =\"strong\">USED TO</span>, followed by the verb in the basic form.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Examples: <br />", "type": "text"}, {"content": " <span class=\"italic\">Many people would criticize Indira Gandhi.<br /> This leader would only think of his own popularity Gandhi used to be a symbol of hope in India.<br />  Indira's streak of gray hair used to be famous.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " When you use the expression USED TO in the negative form, you use the auxiliary DID. Look at the change in the expression:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Some people didn't use to like her ideas. <br />I didn't use to know anything about Indian history.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use <span class =\"strong\">WOULDN'T</span> for the negative form of the expression:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The Sikhs wouldn't follow Indira Gandhi when she was the prime minister.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">WOULD</span> is usually supported by a time expression for the past habit:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">During her time as prime minister, Gandhi would only think of her own popularity.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "political figure"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who is important to the government of a country"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Indira Gandhi became a national political figure. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about the different jobs people have. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "president"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the official leader of a country that does not have a king or queen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She was the president of her party."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "minister"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who is in charge of a government department"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She served as Minister of Information and Broadcasting."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "trademark"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a specific thing about someone which can easily be identified by others"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Her trademark was the streak of gray hair."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dictator"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who rules with complete power in a country"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some thought she was a dictator."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bodyguard"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone whose job is to protect an important person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She had many bodyguards."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to assassinate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to kill an important person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Indira Gandhi was assassinated. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob06aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to succeed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be the next person to take a position or job after someone else"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Her son succeeded her as Prime Minister."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob06aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "controversial"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "causing a lot of disagreement, because many people have strong opinions about the subject"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She remains a controversial figure in Indian politics"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob06aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to influence"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to affect the way someone or something develops, behaves, without directly forcing them"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  She influenced the character of India."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob06aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go on the Internet.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find a female prime minister (living or dead).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Answer these questions:<br/> a. Which country were they the prime minister of?<br/> b. How long were they prime minister for?<br/> c. What other jobs did they have before they became prime minister?<br/> d. Were they famous? What for?<br/> e. What do you think of them?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down all your answers. Share them with your class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I describe a prime minister.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about jobs and work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about past experiences.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}